ing approval. Individual corrections keep deliberate exclusions, original source coordinates, full unchanged Notes and reviewed box relationships.</p><p>Source-row advice still describes the original extracted wording; compare it with the corrected proposal and actual source. A field correction is not a quantity verification or proof that a row belongs in stock. Source Counted columns remain Notes. Reapplying mapping replaces mapped corrections; editing the complete mapped TSV can reset selection and clear provenance, as its notice explains.</p></section><footer class="topic-footer"><strong>Wavelink · AJ Offshore Solutions</strong><p>Product support: <a href="mailto:support@mywavelink.com">support@mywavelink.com</a></p><p>Use your organisation’s approved procedures. This guide does not authorise operations.</p></footer></div><p id="ui111-inventory-review-safeguards"><strong>Keep corrections while reviewing worksheets.</strong> Switching <strong>Inspect worksheet</strong> only changes the worksheet you are inspecting. A completed check, its import overview and your confirmation stay available. Changing included sheets, locations, destination or item fields still requires <strong>Check edited draft</strong> again. Before <strong>Apply mapping</strong> replaces manually corrected names, SN/PN, quantities or box relationships, review the warning for that worksheet. Cancel keeps the corrected rows. Confirm replaces corrections for that worksheet with mapped source values and requires another check. During an uncertain save, retry the unchanged request before changing the proposal.</p><p id="ui112-inventory-review-navigation"><strong>Navigate the inventory review.</strong> <strong>Inspect worksheet</strong> and each worksheet’s <strong>Inspect mapping and items</strong> button change only the sheet on screen. <strong>Worksheets to import</strong> shows the checkboxes that decide what will be saved; an excluded worksheet remains available for inspection. The review shortcuts open Worksheets, Mapping, Items, Boxes, Source or an available Import overview without changing the proposal. Source-column choices show column numbers so repeated headings can be distinguished. A pending-mapping notice explains that current item rows still use the last applied mapping. Review shared-column advice when two destination fields use the same source column; deliberate reuse remains available. Choose an item-name column before applying a mapping.</p><p id="ui113-inventory-mapping-recovery"><strong>Undo pending mapping choices without replacing corrected rows.</strong> <strong>Restore last applied mapping</strong> restores the recorded header and column choices for the worksheet you are inspecting. Current item edits, full Notes, row exclusions, source references and box relationships stay in place. The pending changes show which destination fields or header were changed. Restoration does not apply source values to the rows and requires <strong>Check edited draft</strong> again before saving. <strong>Apply mapping to rows</strong> still replaces mapped values and asks before replacing deliberate corrections. The restore action is unavailable if this draft has no recorded last-applied mapping; older drafts are not guessed from their item rows. Busy or uncertain saves remain locked; resolve an uncertain result with the unchanged retry.</p><p id="ui114-inventory-worksheet-overview"><strong>Review mapping across worksheets.</strong> Each card in <strong>Worksheets to import</strong> shows its current mapping status and row choices. The summary names included worksheets with pending mapping and separates missing-name or unavailable-choice advice. <strong>All worksheets</strong>, <strong>Included</strong> and <strong>Needs mapping</strong> only filter the cards on screen; they do not add or exclude worksheets, switch the worksheet being inspected, or change a completed check and confirmation. Needs mapping can show excluded worksheets too. Their advice does not require adding them to the import. Use <strong>Inspect mapping and items</strong> to inspect a specific worksheet. Apply or restore pending mappings on included worksheets before checking again. A missing source name column is mapping advice; manually edited rows still need comparison with the source and a fresh check. An older draft without a recorded applied mapping remains explicitly unavailable for restoration.</p><p id="ui115-inventory-worksheet-overlap"><strong>Review possible overlap across worksheets.</strong> Open <strong>Review possible overlap</strong> to compare exact matching serial numbers (SN) or asset references in included rows from different included worksheets. Each match remains a separate record. Locations and part numbers provide context; matching part numbers or names alone do not identify overlap. Leading zeros and letter case remain significant. These suggestions are not a stock verification or a duplicate verdict. Excluded worksheets and rows are outside this comparison, and items with neither identifier cannot be compared. Pending mapping choices have not changed the displayed rows. Full mapped-row editing can make the original source row unavailable. Use <strong>Inspect items</strong> to review the current worksheet, or <strong>Inspect source row</strong> where a unique original Excel row is available. These controls preserve a completed check and confirmation. Review the original file when source provenance is unavailable. No rows are merged, removed or excluded automatically. If you edit the proposal, use <strong>Check edited draft</strong> again before saving.</p></main></body></html>--- a/docs/user/topics/inventorybuilder.html
